## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to design a streaming, per-tenant UI with time-based playback, memory controls, and precise cleanup when tenants switch. It exercises useSyncExternalStore, memoized selectors keyed by (tenantId, timeWindow), bounded ring buffers to cap memory, React.memo for EventRow components, playback controls (play/pause and seek), and tenant switch cleanup.

## Key Concepts
- useSyncExternalStore for external streams
- memoized selectors keyed by (tenantId, timeWindow)
- Bounded ring buffer to cap memory
- React.memo for EventRow components
- Playback controls: play/pause and seek
- Tenant switch cleanup

## Code Example
```javascript
// Stream wrapper using useSyncExternalStore
function useAuditStream(tenantId) {
  const storeRef = useRef(null);
  if (!storeRef.current) {
    storeRef.current = createAuditStore(tenantId);
  }
  return useSyncExternalStore(
    storeRef.current.subscribe,
    storeRef.current.getSnapshot,
    storeRef.current.getServerSnapshot
  );
}

// Memoized selector keyed by (tenantId, timeWindow)
const selectBoundedEvents = memoize((tenantId, timeWindow) => {
  return (events) => {
    const cutoff = Date.now() - timeWindow;
    return events
      .filter(e => e.tenantId === tenantId && e.timestamp > cutoff)
      .slice(-120); // Bounded to 120 events
  };
});

// React.memo EventRow
const EventRow = memo(({ event }) => (
  <div>{event.action} - {event.timestamp}</div>
));

// Panel wiring
function AuditPanel({ tenantId }) {
  const events = useAuditStream(tenantId);
  const boundedEvents = useMemo(
    () => selectBoundedEvents(tenantId, 120000),
    [tenantId]
  )(events);

  return (
    <div>
      {boundedEvents.map(e => <EventRow key={e.id} event={e} />)}
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Purpose
Tests the ability to implement offline-first, real-time collaboration with a patch-based DOM updater and proper sequencing. Covers DOM operations, fetch, WebSocket handling, Service Worker caching, and error handling with reconnection strategies.

## Key Concepts
- Patch-based DOM updates using small, immutable operations
- Per-cell sequencing and out-of-order patch buffering
- Offline-first architecture with Service Worker stale-while-revalidate
- Reconnection strategy with exponential backoff and jitter

## Code Example
```javascript
// REST/WS wrapper with reconnection
class GridClient {
  constructor(url) { this.url = url; this.ws = null; this.seq = {}; }
  async init() {
    const layout = await fetch(this.url + '/grid').then(r => r.json());
    this.render(layout);
    this.connect();
  }
  connect() {
    this.ws = new WebSocket(this.url.replace('http','ws') + '/stream');
    this.ws.onmessage = e => this.process(JSON.parse(e.data));
    this.ws.onclose = () => setTimeout(() => this.connect(), this.backoff());
  }
  backoff() { return Math.min(30000, (this.attempts || 1) * 1000 * (0.5 + Math.random())); }

  // Patch processor with buffering
  process(patch) {
    const { cellId, seq } = patch;
    if (!this.seq[cellId] || seq > this.seq[cellId]) this.pending[cellId]?.push(patch);
    while (this.pending[cellId]?.length) {
      const p = this.pending[cellId].sort((a,b) => a.seq - b.seq).shift();
      if (p.seq === this.seq[cellId] + 1) { this.apply(p); this.seq[cellId] = p.seq; }
    }
  }
  apply({cellId, op, value}) {
    const el = document.getElementById(cellId);
    if (op === 'set') el.textContent = value;
    else if (op === 'add') el.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend', value);
    else if (op === 'del') el.remove();
  }
}
```

